{"title":"Hearthstay","sub":"Biggest city or best city? Choosing the next launch","type":"Market entry","industry":"Travel marketplace","geo":"Portugal","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Marketplace expansion · supply acquisition · payback","prompt":"Hearthstay is a holiday-rental marketplace with a strong position in northern Spain. It wants to launch one new city next year and is choosing between Lisbon, Porto and Seville. The CEO's instinct is Lisbon, the biggest tourist market. The board wants the city that pays back fastest.","clarify":[{"q":"Hearthstay's model?","a":"It takes 15% of each booking. It must recruit hosts (property owners) before guests can book."},{"q":"Host economics?","a":"An active host is booked about 12 nights a month on average."},{"q":"Launch costs?","a":"About $150k per city for a local team and legal set-up, plus the cost of recruiting each host."},{"q":"Competition?","a":"Strong in Lisbon (two big platforms), weaker in Porto and Seville."},{"q":"City data?","a":"Lisbon: 18,000 guest-nights a month, we could win 12%, $120 a night, guest marketing 8% of bookings, $600 to recruit each host; Porto: 8,000 guest-nights a month, we could win 35%, $95 a night, guest marketing 4% of bookings, $250 to recruit each host; Seville: 12,000 guest-nights a month, we could win 20%, $110 a night, guest marketing 5% of bookings, $350 to recruit each host."}],"structure":{"root":"Which city should Hearthstay launch next?","branches":[{"head":"Size of the prize","items":["Demand","Share we can win","Nightly rate"]},{"head":"Cost to build supply","items":["Hosts needed","Cost per host"]},{"head":"Cost to win guests","items":["Marketing as % of bookings"]},{"head":"Payback","items":["Launch cost ÷ monthly contribution"]}]},"hypothesis":"Lisbon is biggest, but with strong competitors Hearthstay would win a small share at a high cost. A smaller city with weak competition may pay back faster.","questions":[{"q":"For each city, work out nights booked, hosts needed and monthly contribution.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["City","Nights a month","Hosts needed","Contribution ($k/month)","Launch cost ($k)","Payback (months)"],"rows":[["Lisbon","2,160","180","18.1","258","14.2"],["Porto","2,800","233","29.3","208","7.1"],["Seville","2,400","200","26.4","220","8.3"]],"title":"Exhibit 1 · City comparison","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p>Nights = demand × share we can win. Hosts needed = nights ÷ 12. Contribution = nights × nightly rate × (15% take − guest marketing %).</p>","note":"Launch cost = hosts × cost per host + $150k."},{"q":"Which city would you choose, and why not Lisbon?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"401.708281pt\" height=\"164.94pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 401.708281 164.94\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 164.94 L 401.708281 164.94 L 401.708281 0 L 0 0 L 0 164.94 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 48.548281 139.04 L 394.508281 139.04 L 394.508281 11.528 L 48.548281 11.528 L 48.548281 139.04 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"109.203606\" y=\"139.04\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(95.946887 155.265) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-29\" d=\"M 3034 0 L 595 0 L 595 4467 L 1133 4467 L 1133 474 L 3034 474 L 3034 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" d=\"M 800 4077 Q 640 4077 563 4157 Q 486 4237 486 4365 L 486 4448 Q 486 457