281 11.528 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_7\"><path d=\"M 48.548281 139.04 L 394.508281 139.04 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(104.403606 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(219.128281 76.12) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(331.452957 65.857465) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" d=\"M 1920 -77 Q 1414 -77 1068 92 Q 723 262 547 556 Q 371 851 371 1216 Q 371 1670 620 1942 Q 870 2214 1274 2323 L 1274 2374 Q 922 2496 714 2768 Q 506 3040 506 3424 Q 506 3936 880 4240 Q 1254 4544 1920 4544 Q 2586 4544 2960 4240 Q 3334 3936 3334 3424 Q 3334 3040 3126 2768 Q 2918 2496 2566 2374 L 2566 2323 Q 2970 2214 3219 1942 Q 3469 1670 3469 1216 Q 3469 851 3293 556 Q 3117 262 2774 92 Q 2432 -77 1920 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2387 390 2643 601 Q 2899 813 2899 1190 L 2899 1325 Q 2899 1702 2643 1913 Q 2387 2125 1920 2125 Q 1453 2125 1197 1913 Q 941 1702 941 1325 L 941 1190 Q 941 813 1197 601 Q 1453 390 1920 390 z\nM 1920 2573 Q 2336 2573 2557 2755 Q 2778 2938 2778 3277 L 2778 3373 Q 2778 3712 2557 3894 Q 2336 4077 1920 4077 Q 1504 4077 1283 3894 Q 1062 3712 1062 3373 L 1062 3277 Q 1062 2938 1283 2755 Q 1504 2573 1920 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p4279c633f3\"><rect x=\"48.548281\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · Payback (months)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Porto</b> pays back in about 7 months: weaker competition means a large share, hosts are cheap to recruit, and guest marketing is low.</p> <p>Lisbon has the most demand, but Hearthstay would win only 12%, hosts cost $600 each to win from rivals, and 8% of each booking goes on marketing, leaving 7% of the booking as contribution. Payback: about 14 months.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> in marketplaces, the best city is where you can become the leader, not the biggest market.</p>"},{"q":"What would you check before committing to Porto?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Seasonality:</b> is demand spread through the year, or concentrated in summer?</li><li><b>Regulation:</b> local short-let licence rules and caps</li> <li><b>Network effect:</b> guests from Spain may book Porto, so cross-promotion could lower guest marketing further</li><li>Whether Lisbon could follow once Porto proves the model</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch in Porto first. It pays back in about 7 months, against about 14 for Lisbon, because weak competition lets Hearthstay win a large share with cheap hosts and little guest marketing. Lisbon is the biggest market, but strong rivals would keep Hearthstay's share small and its costs high. Risks: seasonality and short-let licensing in Porto. Next step: recruit 50 hosts as a pilot before full launch, then reconsider Lisbon once the region is established.","great":["Builds supply needs from demand (hosts per night booked)","Compares payback, not market size","Explains why share matters more than size in marketplaces","Checks seasonality and regulation"],"id":74,"slug":"hearthstay"}